LAN definition: group of devices that will receive a braodcast frame.

Vlans (virtual local area network): used when we want to separate devices on the L2. Subnetting separates them on L3. Vlans are configured on the switch in each interfaces, 
but it is not the switch that does the intervlan routing. When configuring Vlans on the switch, if we want a single vlan on an interface, we configure the interface as an
access port. If we want many vlans on a single interface, we configure the interface as a trunk port.
